# .kb demo — replace or extend; safe to commit to git
# Format: optional # TOPIC: … then ## SUBJECT: …
#   - subject before any TOPIC (or under "# TOPIC: other") → topic **other**
# Refs: kb:topic/subject  or  kb:subject (implies other)
# Metadata:  - created: YYYY-MM-DD   - modified: YYYY-MM-DD (bumped on commit)
# Secrets: obfuscate with context menu .kb - Obfuscate (selection required) → ⟦secret:base64⟧ (not encryption)

# TOPIC: Registry

## SUBJECT: cleanup images
- created: 2026-10-06
- modified: 2026-10-06
Retention then garbage-collect. Dry-run first.

```bash
# example registry CLI — replace with your tool
registryctl retention run --project demo --dry-run
registryctl gc now --dry-run
```

## SUBJECT: robot account
- created: 2026-10-06
- modified: 2026-10-06
Pull-only robot. Token is a mock — hover / ⧉ still works:

- robot token: ⟦secret:cmVnaXN0cnktcm9ib3QtdG9rZW4tbm90LXJlYWw=⟧

```bash
curl -fsS -u "robot\$demo+ci:${REGISTRY_ROBOT_TOKEN}" \
  "https://registry.example.com/v2/_catalog" | jq .
```


# TOPIC: Notes plugin

## SUBJECT: kb refs
- created: 2026-10-06
- modified: 2026-10-06
Inline: `kb:<topic>/<subject>` or short `kb:<subject>` (topic **other**).

```text
kb:registry/cleanup-images
kb:example-ticket
```

Edit a subject from hover / Browse (not by typing in this file). Commit the slice with Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+Enter.


# TOPIC: other

## SUBJECT: EXAMPLE-TICKET
- created: 2026-10-06
- modified: 2026-10-06
Ticket-shaped subject under **other**. Short ref `kb:example-ticket` wins over YouTrack hover while the caret is inside `kb:`.

Follow-ups belong in the daily notes file under `# EXAMPLE-TICKET:`.
